.TH RUSTY-CRUNCH 1 "2026-09-29" "rusty-crunch 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rusty-crunch \- fast, local batch media converter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rusty-crunch
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ FOLDER ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rusty-crunch
is a terminal front-end that orchestrates FFmpeg, ImageMagick, Ghostscript and
LibreOffice to batch-convert and compress audio, video, images and documents.
It can also run as a background agent that watches folders.
.PP
With no options it starts an interactive menu. Supplying
.B FOLDER
skips the folder picker; combining it with
.B \-\-yes
(or an explicit
.BR \-\-mode )
runs fully non-interactively.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Non-interactive mode: use configuration defaults and skip every prompt.
Requires a FOLDER.
.TP
.BI \-\-mode " optimize|upscale|restore"
Non-interactive action. Defaults to
.IR optimize .
.TP
.BR \-\-recursive " / " \-\-no\-recursive
Scan (or do not scan) sub-folders, overriding the configuration default.
.TP
.B \-\-delete\-originals
Delete originals after a successful conversion.
.TP
.B \-\-force\-recheck
Re-process files even if they were previously optimized.
.TP
.BI \-\-quality " low|medium|high"
Output quality for optimize mode.
.TP
.BR \-\-min\-size " SIZE, " \-\-max\-size " SIZE"
Only process files within a size range, e.g.
.IR 10MB " or " 4GB .
.TP
.BR \-\-target " HEIGHT, " \-\-preset " anime|movie"
Upscale target height and profile.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Simulate the run without converting anything.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the conversion summary as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colored output. The
.B NO_COLOR
environment variable and non-TTY output are also honoured.
.TP
.B \-\-history
List recorded conversion sessions, newest first.
.TP
.B \-\-stats
Show cumulative files converted and space reclaimed.
.TP
.B \-\-notify
Send a desktop notification when a batch finishes.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose diagnostics (also written to the log file).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress non-essential output.
.TP
.B \-\-health\-check
Verify the required external tools. Exits non-zero if any are missing.
.TP
.BR \-\-agent ", " \-\-agent\-stop ", " \-\-agent\-status
Run, stop or query the background agent.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-list\-formats
List every supported input/output format and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-check\-update " / " \-\-self\-update
Report, or download and install, a newer release (checksum-verified).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colored output when set to any non-empty value.
.TP
.B RUSTY_CRUNCH_CONFIG
Override the config file path (also relocates the cache, history and log).
.TP
.B RUSTY_CRUNCH_VAAPI_DEVICE
Override the VAAPI render node (default: the first
.IR /dev/dri/renderD* ).
.SH FILES
All state lives in the platform configuration directory, e.g.
.I ~/.config/rusty-crunch
on Linux:
.TP
.I config.json
Settings and agent rules.
.TP
.I opt_cache.json
Optimization cache keyed on file size and modification time.
.TP
.I history/
Restore history and original-file backups.
.TP
.I agent.pid ", " agent.log
Agent lifecycle file and log.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error, missing external tool, or one or more files failed to convert.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Interactive:
.PP
.nf
    rusty-crunch
.fi
.PP
Optimize a folder non-interactively and emit JSON:
.PP
.nf
    rusty-crunch --yes --recursive --delete-originals --json ~/Videos
.fi
.PP
Upscale to 1440p with the anime profile:
.PP
.nf
    rusty-crunch --yes --mode upscale --target 1440 --preset anime ~/Anime
.fi
.PP
Undo the last conversion session:
.PP
.nf
    rusty-crunch --mode restore
.fi
.SH REQUIREMENTS
FFmpeg (audio/video), ImageMagick (images), Ghostscript (PDF) and LibreOffice
(office documents), installed separately. rusty-crunch can auto-install them via
supported package managers.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/pgm1207/rusty-crunch/issues
